CPython test-corpus manifests
=============================

The files under token/testdata/cpython, scanner/testdata/cpython,
ast/testdata/cpython and parser/testdata/cpython are derived from CPython
3.14.9 (https://github.com/python/cpython, tag v3.14.9) and from the output of
a CPython 3.14.9 interpreter run over that source. They are generated by
`make corpus-extract` (internal/cpython/cmd/pycorpus) and must not be edited
by hand.

What is derived:

  - Source snippets and their expected outcomes (token dumps, ast.dump output,
    SyntaxError records) taken from Lib/test (test_ast/snippets.py,
    test_tokenize.py, test_syntax.py and other test modules, including
    doctests) and from calls in those modules that pass a source string to the
    compiler.
  - Paths, SHA-256 hashes of source files, and hashes of dumps for the files of
    Lib/ and Lib/test/. The files themselves are not vendored; they are fetched
    from the tag above into the gitignored .cache/ directory by `make corpus`
    and verified against these hashes.
  - Tables read from the interpreter: token names, keywords, ast node schema,
    Unicode identifier/printable ranges, and repr() of sample constants.

